-- Q1764: Review and Compilation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Issue a compilation report with the omission clearly indicated in the report","Not issue a compilation report under any circumstances","Issue a standard compilation report with no modifications to the language","Issue a review report instead of completing the compilation engagement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 80, the accountant may compile financial statements that omit substantially all disclosures if the omission is clearly indicated in the report and is not intended to mislead users. This is common for internal-use financial statements.
Wrong (B): AR-C 80 does not prohibit issuing a compilation report when disclosures are omitted. The standard specifically permits this with proper disclosure of the omission.
Wrong (C): A standard report without modification would be inappropriate because the omission must be clearly indicated in the report.
Wrong (D): The accountant is not required to change the engagement level; the compilation can proceed with proper disclosure of the omission.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1764;

