-- Q1771: Review and Compilation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Perform additional procedures including further inquiries to resolve the matter","Immediately withdraw from the engagement without further action","Issue a qualified review report without performing further procedures","Convert the engagement to a compilation to reduce the scope"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90.36-.37, when the accountant believes the financial statements may be materially misstated, the accountant must perform additional procedures sufficient to obtain limited assurance. These may include additional inquiries and analytical procedures.
Wrong (B): Immediate withdrawal is premature. The accountant should first perform additional procedures to determine whether a material misstatement exists before considering withdrawal.
Wrong (C): Issuing a qualified report without further procedures would violate the accountant''s responsibility to obtain limited assurance under AR-C 90.
Wrong (D): Converting to a compilation is not the appropriate response to a suspected misstatement; the accountant should resolve the matter within the review engagement.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1771;

-- Q1772: Review and Compilation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The accountant''s signed report on the financial statements","A legend stating no assurance is provided on these statements","The CPA firm''s letterhead and contact information","A statement that the financial statements are GAAP-compliant"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 70.07, when no report is issued for a preparation engagement, each page of the financial statements must include a legend such as "no assurance is provided on these financial statements." This alerts users that no audit, review, or compilation procedures were performed.
Wrong (A): A preparation engagement does not include a separate accountant''s report. That distinguishes it from a compilation or review engagement.
Wrong (C): The CPA firm''s letterhead is not required on each page. The required element is the no-assurance legend.
Wrong (D): The legend does not certify GAAP compliance. It communicates the absence of any assurance on the financial statements.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1772;

-- Q1777: Review and Compilation [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Proceed with the limited review and modify the report accordingly","Evaluate whether the limitation prevents completion and withdraw if so","Downgrade the engagement to a compilation engagement automatically","Issue a standard review report and document the limitation internally"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 90.42-.43, if management imposes a limitation that prevents the accountant from performing procedures considered necessary, the accountant must evaluate whether this results in an incomplete review. If the review cannot be completed, withdrawal from the engagement is appropriate.
Wrong (A): A review report cannot simply be modified to address a scope limitation imposed by management. The accountant must determine if the engagement can be completed.
Wrong (C): The accountant cannot automatically downgrade the engagement level. A change in engagement type requires separate evaluation and a new engagement letter.
Wrong (D): Issuing a standard report while only documenting the limitation internally would misrepresent the scope of work performed.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1777;

-- Q1781: Review and Compilation [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The prior-year compiled statements must be re-compiled under review standards","The prior-year compiled statements may be presented with appropriate reference","The prior-year statements must be audited before comparative presentation","The prior-year statements cannot be presented alongside reviewed statements"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 90.56, when comparative financial statements are presented with different levels of service, the prior-year compiled statements may be presented alongside the current-year reviewed statements. The compilation report should be reissued or an appropriate reference made in the current-year review report.
Wrong (A): There is no requirement to re-compile the prior-year statements. They may be presented as originally compiled with proper reference to the service level.
Wrong (C): AR-C does not require a prior audit for comparative presentation. Compiled statements may be presented alongside reviewed statements without upgrading the service level.
Wrong (D): The standards explicitly permit comparative presentation of statements with different levels of service.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1781;

-- Q1794: Review/Compilation Engagements [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Only if all required disclosures are eventually included in the statements","If the selected disclosures are not misleading and the omission is stated","Only if the entity is a nonprofit organization under special frameworks","It is never acceptable to include selected disclosures with omissions"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 80.22, selected disclosures may be included in compiled financial statements that omit substantially all disclosures, provided the selected disclosures are not misleading and the compilation report clearly states the omission of substantially all disclosures.
Wrong (A): There is no requirement to eventually include all disclosures. The standard permits selected disclosures alongside the omission as long as they are not misleading.
Wrong (C): This permission applies to all entities, not just nonprofits. AR-C 80 does not restrict selected disclosures by entity type.
Wrong (D): AR-C 80 explicitly permits including selected disclosures when substantially all disclosures are omitted, as long as they do not create a misleading impression.$EXPL$
