-- Q1796: Review/Compilation Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Discuss with management, request revision, and consider the report impact","Take no action since the review report has already been issued","Issue an audit report on the revised set of financial statements","Notify the SEC about the material misstatement in the statements"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90.A66, when the accountant becomes aware of subsequently discovered information indicating a material misstatement, the accountant should discuss the matter with management, request revision of the financial statements if appropriate, and consider the effect on the issued review report.
Wrong (B): Ignoring material subsequently discovered information would violate the accountant''s professional obligations under AR-C 90.
Wrong (C): A review engagement does not become an audit. The accountant should address the matter within the review framework, not change the engagement level.
Wrong (D): For nonissuers, the accountant''s obligation is to work with management to revise the financial statements, not to notify the SEC.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1796;

-- Q1797: Review/Compilation Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["When there is reasonable justification such as changed circumstances","Only if the accountant has not yet begun the review procedures","It is never acceptable to downgrade from a review to compilation","Only if the client agrees to pay the original review engagement fee"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90.46, a change from a review to a compilation may be acceptable when there is a reasonable justification, such as a change in circumstances, change in requirements, or a misunderstanding about the nature of the service originally requested.
Wrong (B): AR-C 90.46 does not limit the change to situations where procedures have not begun. A reasonable justification is the key factor, not the stage of completion.
Wrong (C): AR-C 90 explicitly permits engagement changes when there is a reasonable justification. A blanket prohibition would be inconsistent with the standard.
Wrong (D): The fee arrangement is not a relevant factor. AR-C 90.47 focuses on whether the reason is legitimate, not on financial terms.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1797;

