-- Q1801: Review/Compilation Engagements [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Substantially less in scope than an audit and not an opinion","Equivalent in scope to an audit but with different reporting format","Limited to confirming account balances and testing internal controls","Designed to detect all instances of fraud and material error"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90.39, the review report must include a statement that a review is substantially less in scope than an audit, the objective of which is the expression of an opinion regarding the financial statements as a whole. This distinguishes limited assurance from reasonable assurance.
Wrong (B): A review is not equivalent in scope to an audit. It consists primarily of inquiries and analytical procedures, which are substantially less extensive.
Wrong (C): Confirming account balances and testing controls are audit procedures. A review relies on inquiries and analytical procedures, not direct testing.
Wrong (D): A review is not designed to detect all fraud or errors. It provides limited assurance that no material modifications are needed.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1801;

-- Q1802: Review/Compilation Engagements [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["A statement that the review was performed in accordance with SSARS","A paragraph describing each analytical procedure that was performed","A list of all management personnel interviewed during the review","A description of the specific inquiry questions asked of management"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90.36, the review report for a nonissuer states that the review was conducted in accordance with Statements on Standards for Accounting and Review Services (SSARS) promulgated by the ARSC of the AICPA.
Wrong (B): The review report does not detail specific analytical procedures performed. It provides a standard description of the review process.
Wrong (C): The report does not list management personnel interviewed. It describes the nature of the review in general terms.
Wrong (D): Specific inquiry questions are not disclosed in the report. The report states that a review includes inquiries and analytical procedures without itemizing them.$EXPL$
