-- Q1803: Review/Compilation Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Reclassify the debt to current without consulting management first","Discuss with management and consider modifying the compilation report","Ignore the issue since compilations provide no assurance to users","Issue a review report instead of completing the compilation"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 80.20-.21, when an accountant performing a compilation becomes aware of a misclassification, the accountant should discuss the matter with management and request revision. If management refuses to correct it, the accountant should consider modifying the compilation report to disclose the departure.
Wrong (A): The accountant cannot unilaterally change the financial statements. Management is responsible for the financial statements, and changes require their approval.
Wrong (C): While compilations provide no assurance, the accountant cannot knowingly be associated with materially misstated financial statements without taking action.
Wrong (D): A misclassification does not require changing the engagement level. The matter can be addressed within the compilation engagement.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1803;

-- Q1808: Review/Compilation Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Be identical in all respects to an annual review report","Identify the interim information and note management''s responsibility","Include an audit opinion on the interim financial statements","Only be issued if the entity also has an annual audit engagement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 90, the review report on interim financial statements identifies the interim financial information reviewed and notes that the preparation of interim financial information is management''s responsibility. The report also describes the accountant''s procedures and provides a limited assurance conclusion.
Wrong (A): While similar, the interim review report is tailored to interim financial information and differs from an annual report in its specific references.
Wrong (C): A review provides limited assurance, not an audit opinion. Audit opinions require procedures performed under AU-C standards.
Wrong (D): There is no requirement for a concurrent annual audit engagement. An interim review can be performed independently.$EXPL$
