-- Q1813: Review/Compilation Engagements [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Refuse the request because conversion would require audit procedures","Evaluate whether sufficient information exists for accrual-basis compilation","Only convert if the entity has been audited in the prior year","Issue a disclaimer of opinion on the accrual-basis financial statements"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 80, the accountant can compile financial statements on the accrual basis even if the books are maintained on the cash basis, provided sufficient information is available to make the conversion. The engagement letter should be amended to reflect the accrual-basis framework.
Wrong (A): Converting from cash to accrual basis does not require audit procedures. It is an accounting conversion that can be performed within a compilation engagement.
Wrong (C): There is no prior-year audit requirement for basis conversion. The accountant only needs sufficient information to prepare accrual-basis statements.
Wrong (D): A disclaimer is not appropriate for a compilation. The accountant either compiles the statements or declines the engagement.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1813;

-- Q1814: Review/Compilation Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Calculating the depreciation-to-assets ratio and comparing to prior year","Comparing the current-year depreciation expense to total revenue","Confirming the original cost of assets with external vendors","Inspecting asset purchase invoices for proper recording in the ledger"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90.32, calculating the ratio of depreciation expense to gross depreciable assets and comparing it to prior years and expected useful lives helps assess reasonableness. This is an appropriate analytical procedure for a review engagement.
